WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.785
Your agent, in your terminal.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:13.465
One command opens a full screen chat that shows what the agent has loaded, then streams, calls tools, and remembers.

00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:17.026
Answers stream in as formatted Markdown.

00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:21.741
Tool calls show their arguments and timing, and code is coloured by language.

00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:27.006
Type slash and a menu lists every command, grouped.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:30.974
The arrow keys move, typing narrows the list, and enter runs one.

00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:36.582
Press question mark for every key, and type to filter them.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:40.230
Escape stops the agent, and typing while it works steers it.

00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:48.076
Name a conversation, fork it to try another approach, and pick up any earlier one with resume.

00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:54.749
Mention a file with at, run a command with bang, or call a function with hash.

00:00:55.069 --> 00:00:57.139
The output goes with your next message.

00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:01.295
Switch models mid conversation.

00:01:01.615 --> 00:01:06.266
Ping checks that one answers, and context shows how much of the window you have used.

00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:13.749
Make the prompt yours: five styles, and widgets for the branch, the clock and the context.

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:21.510
Slash settings tunes how the chat looks and behaves: the header, spacing, thinking and tools.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.972
It shows where each value comes from, and saves it for this agent or for every agent.

00:01:28.272 --> 00:01:29.253
It remembers.

00:01:29.573 --> 00:01:35.931
Notes about you and its work go into every conversation, and a vault keeps secrets sealed, never shown again.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:47.468
See its skills, six of them shipped with bxAgents, and its sub-agents, connect services like GitHub or Notion, and check the tokens it has used.

00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:56.104
Export a conversation as Markdown or a web page, copy the last answer, or record the screen to share.

00:01:58.404 --> 00:02:05.871
And a wizard that asks what your agent should do, from the model and tools to channels and the look of the chat, then writes the project.

00:02:07.371 --> 00:02:08.523
BxAgents.

00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:11.488
Build your agent, then talk to it in your terminal.

